body:
All four seat slots in the join-game and table views showed "Player" because the display name state was hardcoded to that string, which got sent to the backend when creating or joining a room.

## Changes

- **`MultiplayerLobbyScreen`**: Initialize `displayName` from `lobby.session?.username` instead of `"Player"`, so a signed-in user's username is used by default
- **Sign-in flow**: Added a `useEffect` on `sessionUsername` that auto-fills `displayName` when the session is established post-mount (without overriding anything the user has already typed)
- **Tests**: Updated `createRoom`/`joinRoom` call expectations from `"Player"` to `"smoke-user"` to reflect the new default

```tsx
// Before
const [displayName, setDisplayName] = useState("Player");

// After
const [displayName, setDisplayName] = useState(lobby.session?.username ?? "");

useEffect(() => {
  if (sessionUsername) {
    setDisplayName((prev) => prev || sessionUsername);
  }
}, [sessionUsername]);
```
